run(approvedSafeOwnersHash) on a disposable real mainnet fork
├── Given non-mainnet chain, unapproved owners, wrong threshold/count, module or guard
│   └── It reverts before contract creation
├── Given changed deployed pool/legacy identities
│   └── It reverts before contract creation
└── Given the reviewed real mainnet identity graph on a disposable fork
    ├── It deploys three initialized standard UUPS proxies and a disabled fixed-route executor
    ├── It locks each implementation and grants only the fixed Safe authority
    ├── It leaves risk settings, entries, intake, execution and vault binding unset
    └── It returns the exact separate Safe-only binding target and calldata
